//! fail
// A declaration is a store like any other, so it needs the proof of D17.11. The entry block
// zeroes the slot of an owning local once, and a loop body runs again. The first loop deletes its
// local at the end of the body, so the back edge joins an empty slot and the declaration passes.
// The second loop neither deletes nor moves `leaked`, so the back edge joins a live slot with the
// entry zeroing, and the declaration is an error at the declared name, column 22. The closing
// brace of that body ends the scope of `leaked` while it holds its allocation, so the brace is the
// error of the leak rule too (D17.20). Every build mode gives both errors. A checked build of the
// program trapped at run time at the declaration before the rule of D17.11 became static.
// test/overwrite_oracle_test.py holds both positions in every mode.
fn main() i32 {
    i32 mut freed = 0;
    for (i32 mut i = 0; i < 3; i++) {
        i32 mut* own kept = new(i32);
        *kept = i;
        del(kept);
        freed += 1;
    }
    for (i32 mut i = 0; i < 3; i++) {
        i32 mut* own leaked = new(i32); //! error: cannot prove 'leaked' is empty here
        *leaked = i;
        println(*leaked);
    } //! error: cannot prove 'leaked' is empty at this exit
    return freed;
}
